<title>CANADA: Western Canada fertilizer shipment, inventory - CFI.</title>
<headline>Western Canada fertilizer shipment, inventory - CFI.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1996-10-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Canadian Fertilizer Institute released revised July-to-June shipment and inventory data on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Western Canadian Fertilizer Shipments</p>
<p>	  July to June 1995 vs 1996</p>
<p>Fertilizer	  1994/95	    1995/96	  Pct Change</p>
<p>UREA		  1,073,401 tonnes 1,099,427 tonnes  +2.4</p>
<p>AMMONIUM SULPHATE   205,605	    175,663	  -14.6</p>
<p>ANHYDROUS AMMONIA   511,243	    585,296	  +14.5</p>
<p>AMMONIUM NITRATE    189,216	    197,405	   +4.3</p>
<p>MONONAMMONIUM PHSPAT828,313	    885,718	   +6.9</p>
<p>OTHER*		   92,894	     43,668	  -53.0</p>
<p>TOTAL:		3,049,953	  3,161,753	   +3.7</p>
<p>Inventories on June 30, 1995 vs 1996</p>
<p>Fertilizer	  June 30, 1995    June 30, 1996</p>
<p>UREA		    241,400	    208,726</p>
<p>AMMONIUM SULPHATE    72,898	     83,442</p>
<p>AMMONIUM NITRATE     41,049	     39,923</p>
<p>ANHYDROUS AMMONIA   140,079	     47,330</p>
<p>MONOAMMONIUM PHSPHAT111,997		    0</p>
<p>OTHER*		   17,367	     84,819</p>
<p>TOTAL:		  624,790	    464,240</p>
<p>*other includes other phosphates, sulphur solutions, elemental sulphur, sulphate and mixed fertilizer materials.</p>
<p>-- Gilbert Le Gras 204 947 3548</p>
</text>
